# draft
// FIRST DRAFT (phase 2): rewrite or sign off. Voice: docs/voice.md. Flags: docs/story-drafts.md.
A clerk you've never seen drops a ledger on your table. It is taller than he is. He climbs down off a stool to leave, and takes the stool with him.
"The registry," says Skögul. "Outlaws and oathbreakers. Odin's clerks keep it; Odin keeps the clerks." # speaker: skogul
"If a soul is named in there, they go to Hel, whatever else they did. Look them up by name, then look at the face." # speaker: skogul
She opens it at random. Each page is a column of names, each with a small, careful portrait and a line saying what they did. Most of them broke an oath. One of them moved a boundary stone.
* ["What if the name matches but the face doesn't?"]
  "Then it's somebody else's crime. There are a lot of Bjorns." # speaker: skogul
  # fx: flag asked_namesake
* ["Why would an oathbreaker tell me their real name?"]
  "The dead are bad liars about names. It's the last thing they have." # speaker: skogul
  "Faces, they can't do anything about. Check both." # speaker: skogul
- She taps the broken ring on a thong around her own wrist. It isn't hers.
"They keep the ring they broke. Nobody knows why. When you see one, open the book." # speaker: skogul
"The registry is never wrong," she says. "It's just sometimes about someone else." # speaker: skogul
-> END
